  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies a hybrid quantum–classical uncertainty quantification pipeline where classical ML models use features produced by a parameterized quantum circuit with 4–16 qubits. Classical and hybrid models achieve similar predictive performance (R² ≈ 0.79, RMSE ≈ 0.78, MAE ≈ 0.75), while hybrid variants show different uncertainty behavior (e.g., PICP up to 0.9967 for HQQR) and varying outlier detection sensitivity as qubit count increases.",
  "experiments": [
